column33:
Implement the new tester function enableTimingSetRam() to enable the timing set RAM feature in tp_exec/src/pc_lib_foxn.C as follows:


{noformat}//=============================================================================
// Description: Enable Timing Set Ram feature
int PC::enableTimingSetRam()
//=============================================================================
{
	int lstatus = PC_LIB_RETURN_OK;
	rDebug("Enabling Timing Set Ram feature");
	if ( validateTpFunction( __FUNCTION__ ) )
	{
		return PC_LIB_RETURN_WARNING;
	}
	m_bEnableTimingSetRam = true;
	return (lstatus);
}{noformat}

Add this new function to{{/abts_config_csv/tester_functions_config/tester_functions_config.csv, setup = true}}

This function is applicable in tp_setup() only.

settime function does not work as expected

We want settime to repeat the v-pattern for a specific amount of time. The v-pattern is tied to vset commands, which increases the total time. How settime works is that it has the function "addJBCCVector" jump to address of the beginning of the "cycle" it wants to repeat.

Currently settime has repeated the vset commands everytime. We want to change that depending on how many vset commands there are. If only one vset command is specified then we will change the address of the "start" to after the vset commands. If there are no vset commands the testplan is not usable.

Before doing this I'll need to find / keep track of the total amount of "vset", including its address.

int settimeAddress() {
    int jumpAdrs = 0; // if no settime
    if(m_Runtime) { // if in settime
        if(vsetCounter > 1) { // if there are multiple vsets
            // address becomes the start of the 1st vset
            jumpAdrs = vset1.startAdrs();
        }
        else if(vsetCounter == 1) { // if there is one vset
            // address becomes end of vset
            jumpAdrs = vset1.endAdrs() + 1;
        }
        else { // no vset
            error_and_exit();
        }
    }
    return jumpAdrs;
}

