12/Sep/25 11:21 AM;5ac7ec1b1b5dd37ea53a1405;[~accountid:712020:3a7bafd8-4491-445b-b0ce-b630cb251bde] If {{tp_setup()}} includes the {{setstepmode(SM_POWERON)}} call, then {{vset()}} should only be invoked during step 0. This is because the power supplies remain active across steps, eliminating the need to reapply voltage settings in subsequent steps.

*Example modification to* {{testplan()}}*:*

{noformat}   if (getstep() == 0) {	
	vset("VSET1");
   }{noformat}

In this configuration, {{vset()}} is intentionally omitted from step 1 and subsequent steps. However, the "jump back" address location must still be accounted for to ensure proper flow control and test continuity for the rest of the time specified in{{ settime().}}
